  "body": "In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#the-input-byte-stream one can read\r\n\r\n> A leading Byte Order Mark (BOM) causes the character encoding argument to be ignored and will itself be skipped.\r\n\r\nThe [prescan a byte stream to determine its encoding algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#prescan-a-byte-stream-to-determine-its-encoding) doesn’t mention anything about it. Is it normal? If yes what am I missing?",
